.TH POLECAT-BROWSER 1 "January 2026" "Polecat Browser 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
polecat-browser \- fast and privacy-focused web browser for Debian Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polecat-browser
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ url ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polecat-browser
is a modern web browser built with Qt and Qt WebEngine. It offers tabbed
browsing, multiple windows, bookmarks, history, a download manager, private
browsing, privacy controls and optional study tools.
.PP
It contains no telemetry and no advertisements, and does not send browsing
data to any remote service unless a feature that requires it is explicitly
enabled by the user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-private
Start in a private window. Private windows do not save history, cookies,
cache or form data on this device.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-new\-window
Open the given URLs in a new window instead of an existing one.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIname\fR
Use the named browser profile.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose diagnostic logging.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version number.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/polecat-browser/
Configuration (including \fIpolecat-browser.conf\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/polecat-browser/
Data: the SQLite database (\fIpolecat.db\fR), browser profiles and the saved
session.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/polecat-browser/
Cache, including per-profile HTTP caches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES
Qt logging categories; for example
.RB \(lq polecat.*=true \(rq
enables all Polecat diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Polecat Browser user manual and privacy statement, installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/polecat-browser/ .
